{"band":1,"locale":"en","words":[["to do","I study.","To do — and the engine of Korean vocabulary. Attach it to a noun and you have a verb: 공부 study becomes 공부하다 to study, 사랑 love becomes 사랑하다. Hundreds of verbs are built this way."],["a car","I take the car.","A car. The same syllable is also the word for tea, so 차를 마셔요 is I drink tea and 차를 타요 is I get in a car. The verb tells you which one it is."],["woman","That woman is a doctor.",null],["money","There is money in the wallet.",null],["to be in a place","I'm at home.","Korean uses one word where English uses two: 있다 is both to be somewhere and to have. 책상에 책이 있어요 is the book is on the desk; 시간이 있어요 is I have time. Its opposite is 없다."],["I, me","I'm learning Korean.",null],["words, what someone says","Please choose your words carefully.","Speech — words, what someone says. The same syllable is also the word for a horse, and 말 also ends 한국말, the Korean language. Nothing separates them in writing; 말을 하다 is to speak, 말을 타다 is to ride."],["the Sun","The sun rises in the morning.",null],["home, house","I'm going home.",null],["we, us","We are friends.",null],["a hand","I write by hand.",null],["yes","Yes, that's right.","Three common words are spelled 네. This one is \"yes\". The others are \"your\" (네 책, your book) and the native number four before a counter (네 개, four things). Context separates them; nothing in the spelling does."],["time","I don't have time.","Time in general, and also the counter for hours: 두 시간 is two hours. Do not confuse it with 시, which is the o'clock hour — 두 시 is two o'clock, a different thing entirely."],["dog","The dog is running.",null],["a bird","A bird is flying.",null],["door","I open the door.",null],["a body","I wash my body every day.",null],["room","The room is clean.",null],["to go","I go to school.",null],["the back","I wrote my name on the back of the notebook.",null],["eye","Your eyes are pretty.","The eye. Spelled identically to the word for snow, and in careful speech the two are told apart by length: the snow 눈 is drawn out, the eye 눈 is short. Most speakers rely on context instead."],["clothes","The clothes are pretty.",null],["head","My head hurts.",null],["a mouth","The mouth is small.",null],["water","I drink water.",null],["to not have","I don't have money.",null],["you, informally","Where are you?",null],["rain","It's raining.",null],["leg","My leg hurts.","A leg — yours, a table's, a chair's. The same word also means a bridge, which is why 다리를 건너요 is I cross a bridge and not something anatomical."],["school","The school is big.",null],["face","I wash my face.",null],["I, me in polite speech","I am a student.",null],["an arm","Your arms are long.",null],["song","I sing a song.",null],["book","I read a book.",null],["the moon","The moon is bright.",null],["to see","I watch a movie.",null],["telephone, phone","I answer the phone.",null],["tree","The tree is tall.",null],["why","Why are you late?",null],["a day, 24 hours","The day is long.",null],["human being, person","They are a good person.",null],["here","Please sit here.",null],["the world","The world is wide.",null],["the front","Let's meet in front of the shop.",null],["day","It's a good day.",null],["to be late","The bus was late.",null],["a foot, feet","My feet are cold.",null],["photograph, picture","I take a photo.",null],["a nose","My nose is blocked.",null],["bed","The bed is comfortable.",null],["entirety","Everyone has gathered.",null],["now, the current time","I'm going now.",null],["mountain","I go to the mountain.",null],["hospital","I go to the hospital.",null],["gift","I like the gift.",null],["one","One apple, please.",null],["music","The music is nice.",null],["bag","The bag is heavy.",null],["before","I wash my hands before eating.","Before, in time. Several other words are written 전: 전쟁 is war and shortens to 전, 전기 is electricity, and 전 on a menu is a savoury pancake. As a standalone word before a verb it is the time one — 먹기 전에, before eating."],["store, shop","The shop is closed.",null],["the afternoon","Let's meet in the afternoon.",null],["today","The weather is nice today.",null],["road, path","The road is wide.",null],["coffee, especially the beverage","I drink coffee.",null],["an ear","My ear hurts.",null],["rice, a meal","I eat rice.",null],["picture","I draw a picture.",null],["bus","The bus is coming.",null],["really, truly","Thank you very much.","Really, truly — an intensifier before an adjective, as in 정말 좋아요. On its own, with a rise at the end, 정말? is the one-word question really?, which is how you will hear it most."],["alcohol","I don't drink alcohol.",null],["a time","Please do it one more time.",null],["to come","My friend is coming.",null],["movie, film","The movie is fun.",null],["to buy, to purchase","I buy bread.",null],["a plane","I take the plane.",null],["mum, mummy","Mum is cooking.",null],["a star","The stars are shining.",null],["to know","I know the name.",null],["to be good","I feel good.",null],["medicine","Please take the medicine after eating.",null],["the outside","It is raining outside.",null],["sea, ocean","The sea is wide.",null],["apple","The apple is sweet.",null],["sky","The sky is blue.",null],["meat","I grill meat.",null],["friend","I meet a friend.",null],["hat, cap","I put on a hat.",null],["a thing, an item","I buy things.",null],["dad, papa","Good night, Dad.",null],["shoes","I put on my shoes.",null],["something which is real or true","Is this real?",null],["a birthday","Happy birthday.",null],["fire","A fire broke out on the mountain.",null],["five","Five people came.",null],["food, including drink","Korean food is delicious.",null],["opportunity","It's a good opportunity.",null],["market","I buy vegetables at the market.",null],["a moment","Please wait just a moment.",null],["man","That man is my friend.",null],["cat","The cat is sleeping.",null],["two","The two of us are going together.",null],["to eat","I eat fruit.",null],["the time when something happens","I lived in the countryside when I was young.",null],["summer","I go to the sea in summer.",null],["window","Please close the window.",null],["work","There is a lot of work today.","Work, or a thing that has to be done. The same syllable is the Sino-Korean one — 일 번, number one — and it is the day in 일요일, Sunday, and 삼 일, three days."],["animal","I like animals.",null],["cow's milk","The milk is cold.",null],["travel, a trip","I want to go travelling.",null],["bread","I eat bread.",null],["night","There are many stars at night.","Night. Spelled the same as the word for a chestnut, which is a common autumn snack in Korea, so 밤을 먹어요 and 밤에 자요 are about very different things."],["pants, trousers","The trousers are long.",null],["clock, watch","I don't have a watch.",null],["a test, an exam","I have an exam tomorrow.",null],["problem","There is a problem.",null],["city","The city is very big.",null],["computer","I turn on the computer.",null],["the top","There is a hat on the bag.",null],["the weather","The weather is good.",null],["dinner, the evening meal","I eat dinner.",null],["paper","I draw a picture on paper.",null],["spring","Flowers bloom in spring.",null],["father","My father goes to work.",null],["please, do go ahead","Welcome, please come in.",null],["to live","I live in Seoul.",null],["winter","It snows a lot in winter.",null],["child, kid","The child is laughing.",null],["again","Please say it again.",null],["who","Who is that person?",null],["lunch, luncheon","Let's have lunch together.",null],["when","When are you coming?",null],["to be many","There are many people.",null],["hello and goodbye","Bye, see you again!",null],["sometimes","I sometimes watch films.",null],["a street","There are many people on the street.",null],["over there","Over there is the school.",null],["where","Where is the toilet?",null],["to speak, to talk","Please speak slowly.",null],["a skirt","This skirt is very pretty.",null],["name","What is your name?",null],["chair, sofa","I sit on the chair.",null],["to walk","I walk in the park.",null],["the Earth","The Earth is round.",null],["to ride, to get on","I take the bus.","To get on or into anything that carries you — a bus, a bike, a lift. Two other very common verbs share the spelling: 타다 also means to burn, and to stir something into a drink."],["a wall","I hang a picture on the wall.",null],["park","I walk in the park.",null],["the world","I know many countries of the world.",null],["uncooked rice","I wash the rice and cook it.",null],["an egg","I boiled an egg in the morning.",null],["soup","I eat soup in the morning.",null],["sound","The sound is loud.",null],["thought","That's a good idea.",null],["there","Is anyone there?",null],["the side","Please sit next to me.",null],["son","My son goes to school.",null],["puppy","The puppy is small.",null],["family","I have a big family.",null],["to become","I want to become a doctor.","To become. It is also the everyday word for something working or being allowed: 안 돼요 means that will not do, and 다 됐어요 means it is finished. You will hear those far more often than the dictionary sense."],["a village","The village is quiet.",null],["a ball","I kick the ball.",null],["a cafe","I meet my friend at a cafe.",null],["morning","I get up in the morning.",null],["to give","I give a gift.",null],["to make a phone call","I'll call you later.",null],["flower","The flower is pretty.",null],["autumn","The wind is cool in autumn.",null],["the first time","Nice to meet you for the first time.",null],["map","I look at the map.",null],["a colour","This colour is lovely.",null],["vegetables","Please eat plenty of vegetables.",null],["desk","There is a book on the desk.",null],["doctor","The doctor examines me.",null],["a daughter","My daughter goes to school.",null],["to be visible, to be seen","I can see the mountain.",null],["to be right, correct","This answer is right.",null],["hello on the phone","Hello, who is this?",null],["a little","Just a little, please.",null],["fruit","I like fruit.",null],["a seat, a place","There are no seats.",null],["after","I go to the library after class.",null],["very","It's very delicious.",null],["letter","I write a letter to my mother.",null],["tomorrow","See you tomorrow.",null],["a cow","The cow eats grass.",null],["to be important","Health is the most important thing.",null],["card","I'll pay by card.",null],["a company, an office","I go to the office.",null],["news, word from someone","I have good news.",null],["to be small","The shoes are small.",null],["an egg","I eat an egg in the morning.",null],["a river","The river is very wide.",null],["Korea","I like Korean food.",null],["and, and then","I bought bread. And I bought milk too.",null],["too, excessively","These clothes are too big.",null],["together with","Let's eat together.",null],["to read","I read the newspaper.",null],["kimchi","The kimchi is spicy.",null],["that one","Please give me that.",null],["to be big","This bag is big.",null],["the next, the following","See you next time.",null],["to be so","Yes, that's so.",null],["contact","Please contact me later.",null],["to die","The flower in the pot died because it was not watered.",null],["a dragon","There is a big dragon in the picture.",null],["hotel","I slept at a hotel.",null],["key","I don't have the key.",null],["to be pretty","The flowers are really pretty.",null],["heart, mind","They have a warm heart.",null],["to fly","A bird flies in the sky.",null],["to sleep","I go to bed early.",null],["automobile, car","The car is fast.",null],["to throw away","Please throw it in the bin.",null],["the ground","The ground is wet.",null],["meal","The meal was very good.",null],["a machine","The machine has broken down.",null],["an address","Please tell me the address.",null],["to want to","I want to go to Korea.",null],["train","The train has left.",null],["love","Love is beautiful.",null],["a toothbrush","I bought a new toothbrush.",null],["to search, to look for","I'm looking for the key.",null],["no","No, I didn't go.",null],["study","Studying is fun.",null],["a neck","My neck hurts.",null],["fish to eat","I grilled fish for dinner.",null],["teacher","The teacher teaches.",null],["the news","I watch the news.",null],["early","I get up early tomorrow.",null],["building","That building is new.",null],["mother","My mother is at home.",null],["feeling, mood","How do you feel?",null],["alone, by oneself","I can go alone.",null],["but, however","It's raining. But I'll go.",null],["to write","I write my name.","To write. The same verb also means to use something, to wear a hat or glasses on the head, and — as an adjective — to taste bitter. Four everyday meanings, one spelling."],["to drink","I drink milk.",null],["yesterday","It rained yesterday.",null],["readiness, preparation","Everything is ready.",null],["sorry","Sorry, I'm late.",null],["quickly","Please come quickly.",null],["worry","I have a lot of worries.",null],["a place","I found a quiet place.",null],["a chat","Let's talk for a moment.",null],["a shirt","I wear a white shirt.",null],["to sit, to squat","I sat on the chair.",null],["camera","I bought a camera.",null],["to want","What do you want?",null],["a neighbourhood","Our neighbourhood is quiet.",null],["a refrigerator","I put the milk in the refrigerator.",null],["box","I open the box.",null],["the daytime","It is warm in the daytime.",null],["this","Please give me this one.",null],["to be the same","Our bags are the same.",null],["to think","I think so too.",null],["she, her","She sings well.",null],["to draw, to paint","The child draws a tree.",null],["restaurant","Where is the restaurant?",null],["a knife","I peeled the apple with a knife.",null],["mirror","I look in the mirror.",null],["how","How do I get there?",null],["glass","The glass broke.",null],["a miracle","That was truly like a miracle.",null],["to come out","Water is coming out.",null],["to not know, to be ignorant of","I don't know.",null],["a question","I have a question.",null],["how much, how many","How much is this?",null],["grass","The grass is green.",null],["just now","I arrived just now.",null],["to send, to dispatch","I send a letter.",null],["to put down, to place","I put the bag on the floor.",null],["below","The book is under the desk.",null],["an egg","The bird laid three eggs.",null],["age of a person or other living thing","How old are you?",null],["still, not yet","They haven't come yet.",null],["to not do","I don't drink coffee.",null],["a bank","The bank has opened.",null],["the floor","I wipe the floor.",null],["bathroom","The toilet is clean.",null],["unweaned baby, child","The baby is sleeping.",null],["again","See you again tomorrow.",null],["to be beautiful","The scenery is beautiful.",null],["every day","I write Hangul every day.",null],["station","Let's meet at the station.",null],["to be cute","The puppy is cute.",null],["a week","Let's meet next week.",null],["talk","It's an interesting story.",null],["Seoul","Seoul is very big.",null],["stairs","There are many stairs.",null],["to be sorry","I'm sorry I'm late.",null],["pig, swine","The pig is eating.",null],["so, therefore","It's raining, so I'm not going.",null],["you, politely","I waited for you.",null],["already","It's already all over.",null],["a lot","Please eat a lot.",null],["a bus stop","I wait for the bus at the stop.",null],["a price","The price is high.",null],["taxi","Please call a taxi.",null],["student","There are many students in the classroom.",null],["continuation","It keeps raining.",null],["three","Three friends got together.",null],["the Korean language","Korean is interesting.",null],["treasure","The children are looking for treasure.",null],["newspaper","Please read the newspaper.",null],["an order","Would you like to order?",null],["a chicken","The chicken lays an egg.",null],["a cup","I pour water into the cup.",null],["a fact","That is a fact.",null],["a convenience store","There is a convenience store in front of my house.",null],["younger sibling","My younger sibling is cute.","The one sibling word that does not change with the speaker: anyone younger is 동생, whoever is talking. Add a syllable when you need the sex — 남동생 for a younger brother, 여동생 for a younger sister."],["other, different","Do you have other colours?",null],["to stand","I stand in line.",null],["a price","The price is higher than expected.",null],["to stamp","I stamped it with a seal.","To press something down onto a surface: a seal, a stamp, a fingerprint. The same verb covers taking a photograph — 사진을 찍다 — and dipping food into a sauce, all three from the one idea of pressing."],["rabbit","The rabbit hops.",null],["ten","Please count to ten.","Here 열 is the native Korean ten, the one you use for counting things — 열 개, ten of them. A different 열 means a fever, and the verb 열다 means to open. Same two letters, three unrelated words."],["to grab, to catch","I hold your hand.",null],["a reason","Please tell me the reason.",null],["ice","Please add ice.",null],["a need","I don't need help.",null],["nature","Nature is beautiful.",null],["to receive","I received a gift.",null],["driving","I'm learning to drive.",null],["potato","I boil potatoes.",null],["finger","My finger hurts.",null],["cloud","There are many clouds.",null],["to love","I love my family.",null],["like this","Please write it like this.",null],["information","I look for information.",null],["a kitchen","I cook in the kitchen.",null],["a spring onion","I added a little spring onion to the soup.",null],["to work","My mother works at a hospital.",null],["to bloom","The flowers have bloomed.",null],["use","Please tell me how to use it.",null],["to have a need","I need money.",null],["airport","I arrived at the airport.",null],["parents","A child needs parents.",null],["a medical patient","The patient is resting.",null],["to join, to connect","I joined the two ropes.",null],["swimming","I'm learning to swim.",null],["all, every","Everyone laughed.",null],["grandmother","Grandmother is smiling.",null],["the north","They went north.",null],["together","Let's go together.",null],["to sell","They sell fruit.",null],["to like","I like coffee.",null],["to be all right","I'm fine.",null],["country, nation","Korea is a beautiful country.",null],["apartment building, block of flats","I live in an apartment.",null],["for a stretch of time","I travelled during the school holidays.",null],["to dislike","I don't like cold days.",null],["first in time or sequence","First I wash my hands.",null],["to be thankful","Thank you for helping me.",null],["a beast","There was the sound of a beast in the forest.",null],["an entrance","Let's meet at the entrance of the building.",null],["one's parents","I live with my parents.",null],["tofu","I add tofu and make soup.",null],["to be new","It feels fresh.",null],["to be unable to","I can't swim.",null],["to go out","I'm going outside.",null],["to put, to place","I put the book on the desk.",null],["a forest","You can hear birdsong in the forest.",null],["a dance","They danced on the stage.",null],["the tongue","My tongue hurts, so I can't eat.",null],["working out a total","The calculation is slightly wrong.",null],["to wash clean","I wash my hands.",null],["a towel","I dry my hands with a towel.",null],["to be cool, splendid","Your outfit looks great today.",null],["homework","I finished my homework.",null],["to be grateful","Thank you for helping me.",null],["grapes","The grapes are very sweet.",null],["to open","I open the window.",null],["the end","Please stand at the end of the queue.",null],["most, the most","This one is the best.",null],["a plate","Please take out two plates.",null],["the capital city","The capital of Korea is Seoul.","The capital of a country. A separate 수도 means the mains water supply — 수도꼭지 is a tap, 수도 요금 is the water bill. The two are told apart entirely by what is around them."],["to wait for, to await","Please wait a moment.",null],["cooking","The cooking is delicious.",null],["later","I'll call again later.",null],["help","I need help.",null],["salt","I add a little salt.",null],["to be sweet","This apple is sweet.",null],["a quilt","The quilt is warm.",null],["to end","The class is over.",null],["to touch","Please don't touch.",null],["the south","The south is warm.",null],["a request, a favour","I have a favour to ask.",null],["a vegetable","I eat a lot of vegetables.",null],["an island","We took a boat to the island.",null],["especially","I especially like winter.",null],["no","No, I'm fine.",null],["probably","It will probably rain tomorrow.",null],["a greeting","I said hello.",null],["a moment, short time","Let's rest for a moment.",null],["a title","What is the title of this book?",null],["what, what kind of","What work do you do?",null],["the Internet","The Internet is slow.",null],["bicycle","I ride a bicycle.",null],["sugar","I add a little sugar.",null],["a bee","A bee landed on the flower.","A bee. Two other words are spelled 벌: a punishment, and the counter for a set of clothes — 옷 한 벌, one outfit."],["the won","It is two thousand won.",null],["a start, a beginning","It's a good start.",null],["a class","The class is interesting.",null],["year","I studied for two years.",null],["a spacecraft","The spacecraft rose into the sky.",null],["the stomach","My stomach hurt, so I went to the hospital.","The stomach. Two other common words are spelled 배: a boat, and a pear. 배가 아파요 is my stomach hurts, 배를 타요 is I get on a boat, and 배를 먹어요 is I eat a pear."],["a classroom","The classroom is bright.",null],["a passport","Don't forget to bring the passport.",null],["now, and now","Let's start now.",null],["dollar","It's a hundred dollars.",null],["to pay","I'll pay today.",null],["the best","This restaurant is the best.",null],["a sweet, candy","I eat a sweet.",null],["an umbrella","It rained, so I bought an umbrella.",null],["to take time","It takes an hour.",null],["in person, oneself","I made the cake myself.",null],["a fly","A fly is buzzing around.","The insect. Korean writes the city Paris the same way, so 파리에 갔어요 means I went to Paris while 파리가 있어요 means there is a fly. Nothing but the sentence tells them apart."],["an individual word","I learn a new word.",null],["a young woman","A young woman is asking for directions.",null],["to be tall","The building is tall.",null],["what kind of","What kind of colour do you like?",null],["memory","I can't remember.",null],["to draw a line","I drew a line.",null],["a sock","The socks are warm.",null],["to listen, to hear","I listen to music.",null],["to begin","The class is beginning.",null],["a mobile phone","I charge my mobile phone.",null],["to wear, to put on","I put on clothes.",null],["wallet, purse","I lost my wallet.",null],["the space between","There is a tree between the two houses.",null],["a dream","I had a strange dream last night.",null],["a mobile phone","I lost my mobile phone.",null],["still, even now","I am still waiting.",null],["truck","A truck is passing by.",null],["watermelon","Watermelon tastes good in summer.",null],["to kill","I killed the mosquito that came into the room.",null],["a fish","The fish is swimming.",null],["oil","I fry it in oil.",null],["wind","The wind is cool.",null],["everything, all","How much is it altogether?",null],["handwriting","Your handwriting is lovely.",null],["strength","That child is very strong.",null],["strawberry","I wash the strawberries and eat them.",null],["to solve","I solved the problem.",null],["police","Please call the police.",null],["to meet","We meet often.",null],["countryside, the country","The country air is good.",null],["a pencil","I draw a picture with a pencil.",null],["weekend","I rest on the weekend.",null],["glasses, spectacles","I wear glasses.",null],["elder brother of a female","My older brother is driving.","Korean picks the word for a sibling by the speaker's own gender: a woman calls her older brother 오빠, a man calls him 형. It is also used for an older man a woman is close to, which is why you hear it far outside families."],["older brother of a male","My older brother bought me a meal.","A man's word for an older brother. A woman would say 오빠 for the same person. Like 오빠, it extends to a close older man who is not family at all."],["to be bad","The weather is bad.",null],["hope","Please don't lose hope.",null],["a bowl","I put rice in the bowl.",null],["to run","The child is running.",null],["a road","The road is blocked.",null],["to hang","I hang up the clothes.",null],["something, anything","What is this?",null],["the left side","Please turn to the left.",null],["thanks","Thanks for helping.",null],["husband","My husband cooks.",null],["to make","I make bread.",null],["a moment, an instant","I can't forget that moment.",null],["freedom, liberty","Freedom is precious.",null],["football, soccer","I play football with my friend.",null],["to use","May I use this room?",null],["to dig","I dig the ground.",null],["this time","I'll do it this time.",null],["a cigarette","The smell of cigarettes soaked into my clothes.",null],["to be painful, to hurt","My stomach hurts.",null],["gold","This ring is made of gold.","Gold, the metal. The same syllable also means a scratched or drawn line — 금이 갔어요 is it has cracked — and it opens 금요일, Friday."],["a banana","I eat one banana in the morning.",null],["a side dish","The side dishes are delicious.",null],["a laboratory","I worked in the laboratory all day.",null],["a bone","The dog is holding a bone in its mouth.",null],["to do something well, to be good at","You sing well.",null],["a library","I borrowed a book from the library.",null],["thanks","I said thank you.",null],["once, one time","Please give it a try.",null],["life","Life is precious.",null],["dried laver seaweed","We wrap rice in laver and eat it.","The thin dried seaweed eaten with rice. The same syllable is the commonest Korean family name, and it is also steam rising off something hot — 김이 나요, it is steaming."],["knee","My knee hurts.",null],["to be short","The pencil is short.",null],["just, without any particular reason","At the weekend I just stayed home.",null],["wife, especially one's own","I came with my wife.",null],["a year of age","I am twenty years old.",null],["cheese","I like cheese.",null],["gimbap","I had gimbap for lunch.",null],["to rest","Let's rest a little.",null],["popular song","I like Korean pop songs.",null],["one's hometown","I went to my hometown.",null],["the underground","I go by underground.",null],["a method, a way","There is a good way.",null],["the last one","I took the last bus.",null],["to be easy","Hangul is easy.",null],["to be different","The colours are different.",null],["mistake","It's my fault.",null],["a facial expression","Their expression is bright.",null],["secret","Please keep the secret.",null],["grandfather","Grandfather reads the newspaper.",null],["good luck","Good luck with the exam.",null],["beef","We grilled beef and ate it.",null],["university","I study at university.",null],["to give a hand, to help out","Please give me a hand.",null],["a notebook","I write my name in the notebook.",null],["to put on shoes","I put on socks.",null],["an answer","I found the answer.",null],["four","The four of us are one team.",null],["practice","I practise every day.",null],["please","Please help me.",null],["to be cheap","This fruit is cheap.",null],["a plan","I made a plan.",null],["beer","The beer is cold.",null],["a promise, an appointment","I keep my promise.",null],["but, by the way","By the way, what is this?",null],["to help","I help my friend.",null],["the right side","Please go to the right.",null],["this kind of","This is the first time for such a thing.",null],["peace","We wish for peace.",null],["to be glad","I was glad to hear the news.",null],["to learn","I learn Korean.",null],["to be salty","The soup is salty.",null],["never","Absolutely do not be late.",null],["appearance, figure","Their appearance has changed.",null],["to be excellent